{
    "title": "Parametric Definition of Point Set",
    "pathToSources": "Courses/MathForComputerGraphics/Chapter 1/Block 1/",
    "steps": [
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "We already know that explicit representations let us compute points using formulas like y = x² - 5.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "But sometimes, expressing one variable directly in terms of the other is difficult or impossible.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "For example, the implicit equation of a unit circle x² + y² = 1 would be tricky to rearrange into y = f(x).",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "In such cases, we rather use a parametric definition, where both variables are functions of a third parameter.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Let's see — how could the unit circle be represented parametrically? (note: t ∈ ℝ)",
            "contentType": "Geometry",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "geometry": {
                "isNewScene": true,
                "properties": {
                    "showGridLines": true,
                    "showAxes": true,
                    "showNumbers": true,
                    "gridBounds": {
                        "minX": -1.5,
                        "maxX": 1.5,
                        "minY": -1.5,
                        "maxY": 1.5
                    }
                },
                "geometryObjects": {
                    "Add": []
                }
            },
            "multipleChoice": {
                "answers": [
                    {
                        "text": "x = t, y = 2t + 1",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "That’s the equation of a line, not a circle.",
                        "action": {
                            "actionType": "Geometric",
                            "geometricData": {
                                "isNewScene": false,
                                "geometryObjects": {
                                    "Remove": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "circleParam"
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "id": "parabolaCandidate"
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "Add": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "lineCandidate",
                                            "objectType": "Line",
                                            "lineData": {
                                                "pointA": [
                                                    -3,
                                                    -5
                                                ],
                                                "pointB": [
                                                    3,
                                                    7
                                                ]
                                            }
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "x = t, y = t²",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "That describes a parabola, not the unit circle.",
                        "action": {
                            "actionType": "Geometric",
                            "geometricData": {
                                "isNewScene": false,
                                "geometryObjects": {
                                    "Remove": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "circleParam"
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "id": "lineCandidate"
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "Add": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "parabolaCandidate",
                                            "objectType": "Function",
                                            "functionData": {
                                                "expression": "x^2",
                                                "usage": "Plot2D",
                                                "domainStart": -1.5,
                                                "domainEnd": 1.5,
                                                "steps": 50
                                            }
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "x = cos(t), y = sin(t)",
                        "isCorrect": true,
                        "feedback": "Correct! That’s the parametric form of the unit circle.",
                        "action": {
                            "actionType": "Geometric",
                            "geometricData": {
                                "isNewScene": false,
                                "geometryObjects": {
                                    "Remove": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "lineCandidate"
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "id": "parabolaCandidate"
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "Add": [
                                        {
                                            "id": "circleParam",
                                            "objectType": "Circle",
                                            "circleData": {
                                                "center": [
                                                    0,
                                                    0
                                                ],
                                                "radius": 1
                                            }
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Very well, so we now know that x = cos(t), y = sin(t), where t ∈ ℝ, is the parametric representation of a unit circle.",
            "contentType": "Geometry",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "And the parameter t is what helps us generate points on the circle.",
            "contentType": "Geometry",
            "interaction": "Continue",
            "geometry": {
                "isNewScene": true,
                "properties": {
                    "showGridLines": true,
                    "showAxes": true,
                    "showNumbers": true,
                    "gridBounds": {
                        "minX": -1.5,
                        "maxX": 1.5,
                        "minY": -1.5,
                        "maxY": 1.5
                    }
                },
                "geometryObjects": {
                    "Add": [
                        {
                            "id": "circleParam",
                            "objectType": "Circle",
                            "circleData": {
                                "center": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "radius": 1
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "point1",
                            "objectType": "Point",
                            "pointData": {
                                "position": [
                                    0.7071,
                                    0.7071
                                ],
                                "label": "t = π/4"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "point2",
                            "objectType": "Point",
                            "pointData": {
                                "position": [
                                    -1,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "label": "t = -π"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Now let's practice with some more examples of parametric representations.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Which of these has a parametric form?",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "multipleChoice": {
                "answers": [
                    {
                        "text": "y = 2x + 1",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "This is an explicit form."
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "x² + y² = 9",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "This is an implicit form."
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "x = t, y = t²",
                        "isCorrect": true
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "y = sin(x)",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "This is an explicit form."
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Very well, {[x = t, y = t²] | t ∈ ℝ} is indeed a parametric representation of a parabola.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Let’s take a look at how easy it is to generate points with this representation...",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "We’ll fill out the values step by step. First: what is the y-coordinate when t = -2?",
            "contentType": "Table",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "table": {
                "header": [
                    "t",
                    "x",
                    "y"
                ],
                "data": [
